<assembly
        xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/plugins/maven-assembly-plugin/assembly/1.1.2"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/plugins/maven-assembly-plugin/assembly/1.1.2 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/assembly-1.1.2.xsd">
    <id>www</id>
    <baseDirectory>/</baseDirectory>
    <formats>
        <format>dir</format>
    </formats>
    <!--
        TASK 4.7 RETIRED THE commons.ui.libs CHANNEL FROM THIS DESCRIPTOR.

        What was here, and where it went:

          dependencySet  org.openidentityplatform.commons.ui.libs:*:js  -> /libs   (42 files)
          dependencySet  ...:*:css and ...:*:less                       -> /css    (12 files)
          fileSet        Font-Awesome-4.5.0                            -> /css/fontawesome (8)

        All 62 now arrive from declared npm dependencies. vite.config.js stages them from
        node_modules into target/npm-libs (see NPM_LIBRARY_FILES there), which is the first
        composition source exactly as target/dependencies used to be. Four libraries have no npm
        package under any name and are vendored in src/main/js/libs instead; six files that
        shipped but nothing bound were dropped. The whole table is in NOTES-libs-retire.md.

        THIS DESCRIPTOR IS NOT PACKAGING-ONLY, which is why the note matters. It is also the
        descriptor for the prepare-working-dir execution in this module's pom, so its output IS
        target/dependencies - the first entry in Gruntfile.js's buildCompositionDirs and in
        vite.config.js's COMPOSITION_SOURCES. It therefore still has to produce something.

        WHAT IS LEFT IS CODEMIRROR AND NOTHING ELSE: 4 files under /libs/codemirror and 2 under
        /css/codemirror, from the six fileSets below, fed by the unpack-codemirror execution and
        the CodeMirror:zip dependency. TASK 4.8 decides whether npm codemirror@4.10.0 replaces
        them; until it does they must stay, because EditScriptView.js names all four JS files by
        literal AMD path and styles-admin.less @imports both stylesheets. Delete them before 4.8
        lands and the admin script editor breaks. When 4.8 removes them this whole descriptor,
        the prepare-working-dir execution and composition source #1 go with it - an empty
        composition source is the silent-drop shape, not a harmless leftover.
    -->
    <fileSets>
        <fileSet>
            <directory>${project.build.directory}/codemirror5-${codemirror.version}.0</directory>
            <outputDirectory>/libs/codemirror</outputDirectory>
            <includes>
                <include>lib/codemirror.js</include>
                <include>mode/javascript/javascript.js</include>
                <include>mode/groovy/groovy.js</include>
                <include>addon/display/fullscreen.js</include>
            </includes>
        </fileSet>
        <fileSet>
            <directory>${project.build.directory}/codemirror5-${codemirror.version}.0</directory>
            <outputDirectory>/css/codemirror</outputDirectory>
            <includes>
                <include>lib/codemirror.css</include>
                <include>addon/display/fullscreen.css</include>
            </includes>
        </fileSet>
        <fileSet>
            <directory>${project.build.directory}/CodeMirror-${codemirror.version}.0</directory>
            <outputDirectory>/libs/codemirror</outputDirectory>
            <includes>
                <include>lib/codemirror.js</include>
                <include>mode/javascript/javascript.js</include>
                <include>mode/groovy/groovy.js</include>
                <include>addon/display/fullscreen.js</include>
            </includes>
        </fileSet>
        <fileSet>
            <directory>${project.build.directory}/CodeMirror-${codemirror.version}.0</directory>
            <outputDirectory>/css/codemirror</outputDirectory>
            <includes>
                <include>lib/codemirror.css</include>
                <include>addon/display/fullscreen.css</include>
            </includes>
        </fileSet>
        <fileSet>
            <directory>${project.build.directory}/codemirror-${codemirror.version}</directory>
            <outputDirectory>/libs/codemirror</outputDirectory>
            <includes>
                <include>lib/codemirror.js</include>
                <include>mode/javascript/javascript.js</include>
                <include>mode/groovy/groovy.js</include>
                <include>addon/display/fullscreen.js</include>
            </includes>
        </fileSet>
        <fileSet>
            <directory>${project.build.directory}/codemirror-${codemirror.version}</directory>
            <outputDirectory>/css/codemirror</outputDirectory>
            <includes>
                <include>lib/codemirror.css</include>
                <include>addon/display/fullscreen.css</include>
            </includes>
        </fileSet>

    </fileSets>
</assembly>